    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="vehicle_specialization_note" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=16;" value="Vehicle specialization: disjoint, partial. vehicle_type is the discriminator.&lt;br&gt;Partial because the spec lists the three types only as examples." vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="50" width="700" x="460" y="1180" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="business_rules" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;" value="&lt;b&gt;BUSINESS RULES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• HUB.region ∈ {Northeast, Southeast, Midwest, Southwest, West}.&lt;br&gt;• LANE is a weak entity identified by HasOrigin and HasDestination. Its key is the ordered pair (origin_hub_id, destination_hub_id). The two hubs must differ.&lt;br&gt;• Lanes are reference data, loaded with the hubs. A shipment or departure may use only an existing lane.&lt;br&gt;• VEHICLE.vehicle_type ∈ {BOX_TRUCK, REFRIGERATED_VAN, RAIL_CAR}. It must match the vehicle's single subtype row.&lt;br&gt;• SHIPMENT.weight_kg &amp;gt; 0 and DEPARTURE.max_total_weight_kg &amp;gt; 0.&lt;br&gt;• BookedOnto: a shipment is booked onto at most one departure. Each departure may carry many shipments.&lt;br&gt;• The booking procedure checks the matching lane and remaining weight capacity atomically.&lt;br&gt;• SCAN_EVENT is a weak entity identified by HasScan. Its key is (shipment_id, scan_sequence). The sequence is unique within its shipment.&lt;br&gt;• SCAN_EVENT.status ∈ {RECEIVED, IN_TRANSIT, ARRIVED_AT_HUB, OUT_FOR_DELIVERY, DELIVERED}, ranked in that order.&lt;br&gt;• Scan insertion triggers reject a timestamp earlier than the shipment's latest scan, or a status ranked below its current status.&lt;br&gt;• SHIPMENT.current_status uses the same domain. It is NULL until the first scan and is set by the trigger on every scan.&lt;br&gt;• SHIPMENT.delivery_outcome ∈ {ON_TIME, LATE}, NULL until delivered. ON_TIME if the DELIVERED scan is on or before the end of promised_delivery_date.&lt;br&gt;• A carrier may post scans only for shipments booked onto departures run by its own vehicles (SCAN_EVENT → SHIPMENT → BookedOnto → DEPARTURE → Runs → VEHICLE → Owns → CARRIER). The application checks this, so a shipment must be booked before it can be scanned." vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="560" width="1300" x="40" y="1250" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
  </root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
</mxfile>
